course: dictionary
lesson: 15548
title: Superiority: better, or acting better
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Superiority means being better, stronger or higher in quality than others. A team with superiority in numbers has more players than the other team. Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «The blue team had superiority in numbers, with twelve players to our seven.» The number of players tells you what superiority means here.
explain: Superiority can also be about how someone acts. «She spoke with an air of superiority, as if the rest of us were silly.» The words «as if the rest of us were silly» are the clue. She is not just good at something. She is acting as if she is better than other people, and that is unkind and annoying.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about skill, numbers or quality, or about how someone behaves? If you swap in «being better» and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. If it sounds rude or proud, the author probably means the unkind sense.
fact: Superiority means being better, stronger or higher in quality than others.
fact: Superiority can also mean acting as if you are better than other people, which is unkind and annoying.
fact: «Superiority in numbers» means having more people than the other side.
fact: «An air of superiority» describes someone who looks down on others.
fact: Superiority is uncountable, so we say «superiority», not «a superiority».
exercise: «The blue team had superiority in numbers, with twelve players to our seven.» What does superiority mean here? | Being late for the match | *Having more players, so being stronger | Being worse at the game | Being lost in the park
exercise: «She spoke with an air of superiority, as if the rest of us were silly.» What does this show? | *She thinks she is better than others and looks down on them | She has lost her way | She is cold and tired | She is very happy and laughing
exercise: Priya says superiority means being worse than others. Is she right? | Yes, it means being the same as everyone | No, it means being very quiet | *No, it means being better or stronger, or acting as if you are better | Yes, it means being worse
test:
«The king's army had air superiority, so the enemy planes could not fly.» In this sentence, air superiority means | *Having more power in the sky, so the other side could not fly safely | Having a lot of air in the balloon | Being very cold at the top of the hill | Being slower than the other army
test:
Which action shows an air of superiority? | Helping a friend tie their shoelace | Sharing your crisps with the group | *Telling others they are wrong and that you always know best | Saying sorry after a mistake
exam:
Pick the best meaning of superiority when it describes a sports team. | Being worse than the other team | *Being stronger or better than the other team | Being in the wrong place on the pitch | Being very quiet in the changing room
